    turnFlow: 'There is no trick-play phase. After stake layout and deal, players evaluate hands and declare results. If no sweep combination is declared, counters are awarded for most of a suit and second most of a suit (court cards count 10, number cards by pip). Elder hand precedence breaks ties for most and second-most positions. If the same player holds both top suit totals, they take three corner counters. Five sweep combinations override suit-point awards, ranked highest to lowest: Seven Cards (all seven cards same suit), Four Sevens, Ging (a suit totaling exactly 37 with all cards held in that suit), Gentlemen (all face cards), Bare Shoulders (no face cards). A valid sweep takes all layout counters and the layout is re-dressed for next deal.',
